limit-non-tui-thread-lists-to-recent

Lane: backend

FlatPatch: limit-non-tui-thread-lists-to-recent

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Keep non-TUI thread-list clients restricted to the five most recently updated matching threads while preserving the TUI browsing contract.

Requires: none

Provides: Use the initialized client name to preserve codex-tui list pagination and sorting; other clients ignore supplied cursors, use updated-at descending order with a limit of five, and receive no forward or backward cursor while other native filters remain intact.

Boundary: Only thread/list is restricted; thread search, direct thread reads, native filter validation and storage ownership remain unchanged. Client naming selects presentation scope rather than an authorization boundary.

Verification: The non-TUI list test verifies recency, the five-item limit and cursor removal; TUI pagination and section-order tests preserve full browsing and restart behavior.


